{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Indicates the presence or absence of system dividers between this system and the previous system."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout\/systemdividers"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"systemDividers","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemDividers","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemDividers","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemDividersV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<system-dividers>"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"systemDividers","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLSystemDividers","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemDividersV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"systemDividers","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLSystemLayoutV14systemDividersAA0cF0VSgvp","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout\/systemDividers","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout":{"title":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSystemLayout"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLSystemLayout","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a group of staves that are read and played simultaneously. System layout includes left and right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"margins and the vertical distance from the previous system. The system distance is measured from the bottom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line of the previous system to the top line of the current system. It is ignored for the first system on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"page. The top system distance is measured from the page’s top margin to the top line of the first system. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is ignored for all but the first system on a page."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemLayout/systemDividers":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Indicates the presence or absence of system dividers between this system and the previous system."}],"title":"systemDividers","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemlayout\/systemdividers","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"systemDividers"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSystemDividersV","text":"MXLSystemDividers","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemLayout\/systemDividers"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSystemDividers":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSystemDividers","title":"MXLSystemDividers","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsystemdividers","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSystemDividers"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSystemDividers"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The system-dividers element indicates the presence or absence of system dividers (also known as system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separation marks) between systems displayed on the same page. Dividers on the left and right side of the page"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are controlled by the left-divider and right-divider elements respectively. The default vertical position is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"half the system-distance value from the top of the system that is below the divider. The default horizontal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position is the left and right system margin, respectively."}]}}}